e II/III cases, according to the classifications of Bell                                                                                                                                                                                    | All are VLBW with extremly preterm                                        | 4%                       |\n| Boghossian              | 852 US centers                                                                                                                                 | Infants born                                                                                                                                            | Multiples and infants                                                                                                                                                                  | Large for                                                              | NEC was diagnosed                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Mean and SD                                                               | 7%                       |\n\nTable 1 Characteristics of the included studies (Continued)\n\n| Author/year   | data base studied                           | Inclusion criteria                                                                                     | Exclusion criteria                                                                                                                                                                | Population at risk reported   | NEC case definition                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Comment on VLBW